  data: {
    LLM: "Don't sit on your 2s. Playing a 2 starts a new pile, giving you more 'landing spots' for your other cards. Save your high cards (Kings) for later, as they can only be played on a complete sequence.\n\nHand Thinning: If you have many cards of different suits but similar ranks (e.g., three 7s), wait until a 6 is played to dump all of them onto various piles at once.\n\nStalling: If you see your opponent has only 1 or 2 cards left, and you are in the lead, avoid starting a new sequence with an Ace. Force them to draw from the stock until they happen to have a card that fits an existing pile.",
    Player: "Don't sit on your 2s. Playing a 2 starts a new pile, giving you more 'landing spots' for your other cards. Save your high cards (Kings) for later, as they can only be played on a complete sequence.\n\nHand Thinning: If you have many cards of different suits but similar ranks (e.g., three 7s), wait until a 6 is played to dump all of them onto various piles at once.\n\nStalling: If you see your opponent has only 1 or 2 cards left, and you are in the lead, avoid starting a new sequence with an Ace. Force them to draw from the stock until they happen to have a card that fits an existing pile.",
