    basic: "Don't sit on your 2s. Playing a 2 starts a new pile, giving you more 'landing spots' for your other cards. Save your high cards (Kings) for later, as they can only be played on a complete sequence.",
    intermediate: 'Hand Thinning: If you have many cards of different suits but similar ranks (e.g., three 7s), wait until a 6 is played to dump all of them onto various piles at once.',
